//
// PROBE: the `*` fold family (D12) — `*+`, `*-`, `**`, `*/`, a `.` form, and
// `Σ` for `*+`.
//
// One function serves them all
// (reference/rust_multistackvm/src/stdlib/math/math_op.rs:22-76). It folds the
// stack into an accumulator with the ordinary binary operation, operands in
// the same order `+` takes them, until the stack runs out or reaches a NODATA,
// which it consumes (:43-50). The `.` form keeps the accumulator on the
// workbench. `Σ` aliases `*+`
// (reference/rust_multistackvm/src/stdlib/create_aliases.rs:38).
//
"probe: each fold consumes the stack" println
1 2 3 4 *+ println
2 3 4 ** println
100 2 5 */ println
10 3 1 *- println
1 2 3 Σ println
"probe: a NODATA stops the fold and is consumed" println
10 nodata 2 3 *+ println
println
"probe: the . form accumulates on the workbench" println
1 2 3 . *+. debug.display_workbench
